## Title: EasyMark
## Author: Th3rtythr33
## Version: 1.01
## AddOnVersion: 101
## APIVersion: 101051
## SavedVariables: EasyMarkSavedVars
## DependsOn: LibHarvensAddonSettings>=20200
## Description: Places a group target marker on whatever is under your reticle when a trigger you choose fires: starting a heavy attack, swapping weapon bars twice, or using a chosen ability slot or your ultimate.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; MANIFEST NOTES
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; AddOnVersion is an integer that must only ever INCREASE, and it steps by one
; per PUBLISHED build regardless of how far the semantic Version jumps. It is
; what the console catalogue and the PC .addon/.txt tie-break use; Version is
; only ever shown to humans. Build 0.2 shipped to Bethesda.net as AddOnVersion
; 100 (an early mistake, but it is out there), so every later build is 101+.
;
; .addon only, no .txt. Since June 2025 the console client ignores .txt
; manifests entirely; a .addon manifest also loads on PC, so one file covers
; both. Never ship both: PC loads whichever has the higher AddOnVersion and
; equal versions are undefined.
;
; PlayStation's filesystem is case-sensitive. Every path listed below, and the
; folder and manifest names themselves, must match the real files exactly.
;
; Description must stay ONE line and should match the Bethesda.net listing.
;
; DependsOn (hard), not OptionalDependsOn: LibHarvensAddonSettings is on the
; Bethesda.net console catalogue, so a hard dependency resolves and
; auto-installs. The minimum version is pinned to the library's LATEST release
; (2.2.0 = 20200) per ESOUI best practice; raise it whenever LHAS updates.
; On Bethesda.net the dependency is attached to the add-on entry without
; choosing a release.
;
; APIVersion tracks the live game. 101051 = Update 51, live 2026-09-28.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

